A pupil wants to show, by experiment, that two resistors connected in parallel have a smaller combined resistance than either resistor on its own.
Describe how the pupil could do this with a battery, an ammeter and a voltmeter, and explain the result.
Your answer should include:
• where the ammeter and the voltmeter are connected;
• the readings taken, and how the resistance is found from them;
• what is changed between the two sets of readings;
• what the results show, and why adding a resistor in parallel lowers the total resistance.
This question also assesses the quality of your written communication, including your use of specialist scientific terms.
